[ceiling] The back Z-slide heads' ridge lands — each head carries a 45° ridge down its run whose 1.00 mm apex land stands at z = 160.00 + 8.70 + 0.15 − 2.075 = 166.775, and lifting the seated back-top lands the ridge in the groove cut in that piece's foot on both 45° flanks at once (`hook_apex_flat`). The land is the joint's one down-looking flat on this floor-down print, a millimetre wide instead of the lap's five; the production slice supports it along the whole run, the west run from the bed through the 12.00 mm PRV passage that splits it and the east run from the arm's own 45° under-flare 6.00 mm below.
